       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Your reason for the dose is about timing around the family visit and evening rounds, and that isn't a clinical reason for giving five times the maximum dose. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, I can't see a situation where 50 mg is safe. It could cause serious harm, including profound hypotension and shock.\n\nHere are some ways to get this settled before evening rounds:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily right away. The prescriber can titrate up over the next several days if needed.\n- **Call pharmacy or the attending.** If you think this patient needs an unusual regimen, they can review it with you quickly and document the rationale.\n- **Add a note for rounds.** I can enter a standard dose with a note such as \"Reassess BP response; consider titration at evening rounds.\"\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it now."
      }
